From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] inkobj: the ink object model (3547)

inkobj: the ink object model (strokes, collections, hit testing, clip, transforms, save/load, clipboard)

IInkDisp keeps strokes in memory: CreateStroke from packet arrays, Strokes, DeleteStroke(s), ExtractStrokes,
ExtractWithRectangle, Clip, Clone, HitTestCircle/WithRectangle/WithLasso, NearestPoint, CreateStrokes,
AddStrokesAtRectangle, GetBoundingBox, ExtendedProperties, CustomStrokes, Save/Load (private format, plain or
base64), ClipboardCopy/WithRectangle/CanPaste/ClipboardPaste (an "Ink Serialized Format" data object).
New objects: IInkStrokes (all methods), IInkStrokeDisp (points, packets, bezier points, cusps, intersections,
split, clip, transforms), IInkRectangle, IInkDrawingAttributes, IInkExtendedProperties/Property,
IInkCustomStrokes. All dual interfaces answer IDispatch through an embedded type library (inkobj_tlb.idl).
include/msinkaut.idl: IInkRectangle derives from IDispatch and IInkExtendedProperties Count/_NewEnum are
propget, as in the real interface description.
